  "investigation_notes": "Uploads are failing because the app cannot reach its database dependency.\n\n**Symptom - app unhealthy:**\n- `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` (E1) (E5), but `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- App logs for both `upload` at `/app/main.py line 65` and `health` at `line 113` fail in `psycopg.connect(DATABASE_URL)` with `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` (E3).\n\n**Root cause - DB network detachment, not app code:**\n- App is attached to `[\"incidentlab_default\"]` (E5).\n- DB `incidentlab-db-1` is attached to `[]` - no networks (E6).\n- Therefore `db` hostname cannot resolve from the app, matching (E3).\n\n**Dependency itself is healthy:**\n- DB `status running`, `health healthy` (E6) (E1).\n- DB logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` (E8).\n- `pg_isready` checks returned `exit_code 0` and `health_status: healthy` (E7).\n\n**Ruled out storage / permissions:**\n- Bind-mount `/srv/lab-data -> /data rw: true` is present (E5).\n- `/srv/lab-data` filesystem `use_percent 9.0%`, `available_mb 410.7` (E4), `/` filesystem `use_percent 6.8%` (E10) - not full.\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_uid 1000`, `app_user_can_write true` (E9) - writable by app user `1000:1000` (E5) (E9).\n- App `oom_killed false`, `exit_code 0`, `restart_count 0` (E5), DB same (E6).\n\n**History supporting recent change:**\n- Both containers `Up 9 seconds` / `Up 14 seconds` (E1), `started_at 23:38:37Z` / `23:38:31Z` (E5) (E6).\n- `recent_events` shows `kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start/create` for both containers at `23:37:48` and `23:38:31` (E7).\n\nConclusion: uploads stopped as symptom of app `503` (E2) caused by loss of network connectivity to `incidentlab-db-1` (E5) (E6) resulting in DNS resolution failure (E3), while DB and storage remain healthy/writable (E6) (E8) (E4) (E9) (E10).\n",
